---
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import HeroAtmosphere from '../components/HeroAtmosphere.astro';
import PostHog from '../components/posthog.astro';
import '../styles/design-system.css';
import '../styles/components.css';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" /><meta name="description" content="Create an atmosphere for your space with Aether. Try relaxation sessions or customise and save a reusable scene." /><title>For your space — Aether</title><link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" /><PostHog /></head>
<body>
<SiteHeader />
<main id="main">
 <section class="space-hero" aria-labelledby="space-title">
  <div><p class="eyebrow">For your space</p><h1 id="space-title">Create an atmosphere you can return to.</h1><p>Choose a scene, shape its sound and motion, and make room for a quiet moment. Start with a relaxation session or save an environment to use again.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/studio/guided-relaxation/">Choose a relaxation session →</a><a class="button secondary" href="/studio/">Browse scene library →</a></div></div>
  <HeroAtmosphere />
 </section>
 <section aria-labelledby="ways-title"><p class="eyebrow">Choose how to begin</p><h2 id="ways-title">A session for now. A scene to reuse.</h2><div class="space-grid">
  <article><h3>Take a personal moment</h3><p>Choose 5, 10 or 20 minutes, or an untimed session. Use optional on-screen guidance and sound where available.</p><a href="/studio/guided-relaxation/">Open relaxation sessions →</a></article>
  <article><h3>Make an environment your own</h3><p>Open a scene in the editor, adjust its available sound and visual controls, and save your version in this browser for next time.</p><a href="/studio/">Choose a scene to edit →</a></article>
 </div></section>
 <section class="exploring" aria-labelledby="exploring-title"><p class="eyebrow">Exploring together</p><h2 id="exploring-title">Beyond your own screen</h2><p>We’re exploring how reusable environments could support facilitator-led relaxation, venue ambience and sensory or learning experiences in schools, museums and attractions. These are ideas for testing with people who work in those settings.</p><p>Have a particular space in mind? Start with a scene and consider the sound, motion and controls the people using that space would need.</p></section>
</main>
<SiteFooter />
</body>
</html>
<style>
main{width:min(1180px,calc(100% - 3rem));margin:auto;color:#f8fafc}section{padding:clamp(2.5rem,6vw,5rem) 0}.space-hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:center;gap:3rem}.eyebrow{color:#7dd3fc;font-size:.75rem;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase}h1{font-size:clamp(2.4rem,5vw,4.4rem);line-height:1.06;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:1rem 0}h2{font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3vw,2.6rem);line-height:1.15}h3{font-size:1.4rem}p{color:#b9c7d9;line-height:1.75}.actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;margin-top:24px}.space-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px}article{padding:28px;border:1px solid #334155;border-radius:18px;background:#101827}a{color:#7dd3fc}a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #7dd3fc;outline-offset:4px}.exploring{border-top:1px solid #334155;max-width:850px}@media(max-width:800px){.space-hero,.space-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.space-hero{gap:2rem}} 
</style>
